  "reason": "The strongest evidence is that RNA-only scvi_n200 with multiprofile is much better than PCA or scGPT, and avgpool/transformer are nearly tied, with avgpool being simpler and robust. Image-only models are weak, so it is unclear whether image data can add value. This experiment tests whether adding a ViT image branch to the strong scvi multiprofile RNA model improves validation accuracy/F1 over the RNA-only baseline using a simple concat fusion. It is the best next step because it exploits the best RNA evidence while beginning multimodal exploration with the simplest informative fusion setting, reducing uncertainty about whether image information is useful before testing more complex fusion or aggregation choices."
